        <body>
            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0340" n="224" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg224"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1141.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Legation of the Dominican
                            Republic to the Department of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Memorandum—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p>In confirmation of our conversation of this afternoon, I have the honor to advise
                    you that my Government in a cablegram of to-day’s date, informs me that it has
                    declared General Desiderio Arias an outlaw, charging him with being a
                    smuggler.</p>
                <p>My Government also informs me that President Bordas will leave with the troops in
                    order to attack General Arias for the purpose of bringing him to order; that the
                    Dominican Government, in this campaign, counts upon the Department (of State) to
                    lend it its moral support, facilitating the means through which President Bordas
                    may obtain the necessary resources.</p>
                <p>The Government is confident that if these funds are obtained in time, it will
                    easily control the situation, and if it does not obtain them the country will be
                    threatened by anarchy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the Dominican Republic</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-04"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">April 4, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
